<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46398" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suffectĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subf-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		sufficio (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An adding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unguentorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 166</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">macularum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7, 251</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A supplying</i>, <i>substituting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animarum alterna mortuorum atque viventium
					suffectio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 28</span></i>
			; cf. suffectura.</div>
